  "body": "## What changed\n\nFirst slice of #3330: the 5-Axis Contour (`Contour5D`) takes a start point and an exit point. MultiAxisContour is not in this PR. It uses a different planner (the drive-curve `contour_curve`), and the issue asks for one kind for each PR.\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/pick_kinds.rs`: `Contour5D` is now `PickCapability::Ring`. The UI rows, the MCP `edit_operation` schema and `list_operation_types` read this capability, so they take the picks with no other change.\n- `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/ring_seam.rs` (new): `RingSeam`, `waterline_seamed`, and the law. `waterline` moves into this file with the same body.\n- `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/rings.rs`: one hook for the start and one hook for the exit in the ring loop (`emit_rings_seamed`). `None` walks every ring as before.\n- `crates/motion/src/multiaxis/contour5d.rs`: `contour5d_seamed`. The same stamp poses the seated ladder.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`: the Contour5D arm reads `RingSeam::of(&params.path_picks())`. The arm is shared with Parallel5D, and Parallel5D does not read the seam.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3330-contour5d-picks.md`.\n\n## The law (Contour5D)\n\n- Start: each closed ring of the waterline ladder starts at its point nearest the pick (XY). The seams of all levels align toward the pick. The ladder does not read the pick Z.\n- Exit: each closed ring cuts its full lap. Then it continues along its own vertices to its point nearest the exit pick, and the tool retracts there.\n- An open run (a ring that the overhang column law cut into pieces) keeps its ends.\n- The cut order and the cut geometry do not change. Only the seam moves, and the exit adds a re-trace over cut material.\n- The tilt limit, the shank dodge and the centre-cutting guard run on the seated path. Thus they are judged at the pick too.\n\n## Refusals (by name, the pick is never moved)\n\n- `start point (x, y) is d mm from the nearest ring of the ladder, farther than the L mm a start point may sit from it` (L = 1.5 tool diameters). The same text applies for the exit.\n- `start point (x, y): the ladder has no closed ring to start on`. The same text applies for the exit.\n- `start point (x, y): the plunge column to the ring at z Z crosses the part there`. Without a pick, the loop rotates the entry to a clear vertex. With a pick, it refuses.\n- `exit point (x, y): the retract column from the ring at z Z crosses the part there`. The column is judged up to the clearance plane.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` `multiaxis` (module `multiaxis/seam.rs`):\n  - `contour5d_start_point_seats_every_ring_at_the_pick`\n  - `contour5d_exit_point_ends_every_ring_at_the_pick`\n  - `contour5d_exit_point_under_a_canopy_is_refused_by_name` (new)\n  - `contour5d_pick_far_from_every_ring_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `contour5d_without_a_pick_is_the_automatic_ladder_byte_for_byte`\n  - `cuts_ride_the_ladder` samples each level cut every 0.25 mm and requires each sample on the automatic ladder within `TOL`. Before, it read only the end point of each move.\n- `camcraft-motion` lib (`finishing3d::ring_seam_tests`, new):\n  - `exit_retract_column_through_a_canopy_is_refused_by_name`: the exit retract column law on the untrimmed ladder, with a canopy above the exit point.\n  - `nearest_states_a_segment_end_as_the_next_segment`: a foot at a segment end is the start of the next segment, so the run-on adds no lap at the seam.\n- `camcraft-app` `start_exit_shared` (module `start_exit_shared/contour5d.rs`):\n  - `contour5d_starts_at_the_picked_start_and_leaves_at_the_picked_exit`: now also samples each level cut of the started and the picked ladder every 0.25 mm against the automatic ladder (within the 0.1 mm operation tolerance).\n  - `contour5d_refuses_a_pick_far_from_every_ring_by_name`\n  - `contour5d_picks_ride_edit_operation_and_undo_restores_them` (MCP `edit_operation`, `undo`, `redo`)\n  - `every_kind_has_one_pick_capability_and_only_the_taken_ones_take_a_pick` (updated: Contour5D is Ring)\n\n## Mutations (review of `9d11b0ae5`)\n\nEach mutation was applied locally, run, and reverted. None is committed.\n\n| # | Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 | `ring_seam.rs` `run_on`: `poly.extend(lap)` removed | RED: motion `contour5d_exit_point_ends_every_ring_at_the_pick` (\"a cut stands 0.165 mm off the automatic ladder\"), app `contour5d_starts_at_the_picked_start_and_leaves_at_the_picked_exit` (\"a cut stands 0.160 mm off the automatic ladder\") |\n| 3 | `rings.rs`: the exit retract column check removed | RED: motion lib `exit_retract_column_through_a_canopy_is_refused_by_name` |\n| 4 | `ring_seam.rs` `nearest`: the snap at `t = 1` removed | RED: motion lib `nearest_states_a_segment_end_as_the_next_segment` |\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. A path without a pick passes `None` to the ring loop. This is pinned byte for byte at motion scale, and the example catalog suites are green (see the gate).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The blocked plunge column refusal at a picked start has no pinning fixture. Without it, the loop falls back to the old rotation to a clear vertex, which is safe.\n- Through `waterline_seamed`, the exit retract column refusal cannot be reached: the column trim checks the same column every 0.25 mm at an equal or larger radius, so a canopy opens the ring first and the exit pick has no closed ring (pinned by `contour5d_exit_point_under_a_canopy_is_refused_by_name`). The exit law is pinned on the untrimmed ladder.\n- The other multi-axis kinds stay `PICK_OWED`: MultiAxisContour, Parallel5D, Swarf, AdvancedSwarf, RotaryContour, RotaryParallel, RotaryOffset, MultiAxisRough, Flow5D.\n- No machine run.\n\n## Gate\n\nAll on the final head `fdce232c8`, local Mac. The branch has `origin/main` merged in: one conflict in `crates/app/tests/start_exit_shared.rs` (the Gate map header and one panic text of the capability test). Both sides kept; the panic text is main's.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 215 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (29.1 min). The plan includes `motion suites: lib`, `motion suites: multiaxis`, `app suites: start_exit_shared`, and the example catalog suites by name: `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (6.1 min).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean (on `e344b7aba`; the last commit changes only the decision file).\n\nHeavy step: none. This is a P2 issue, and AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a targeted heavy step only to a P1 PR under the safety floor.\n\nChangelog: The 5-Axis Contour takes a start point and an exit point: each closed waterline ring starts at its point nearest the start pick and, after its lap, leaves at its point nearest the exit pick; a pick that cannot be held is refused by name.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #3330\n\n",
